-- title:
--   Summing the squared terminal coordinates over sketch states
-- statement:
--   Assume the native core state contains the terminal dense graph-sketch matrix $D_k$, the state index is zero, the label counter contains $k$ unary markers, the predecessor counter is empty, and the norm accumulator is its empty prefix value. The norm loop consumes the label counter, sets the index to $k$, and computes
--   $$\sum_{a<k}\left(\sum_{v<n}D_k(v,a)_{[k]}\right)^2.$$
--   Here $[k]$ is the full set of exterior coordinates. Other native state and original tails are preserved. Its time is bounded by $(\operatorname{normStateCost}(n,k)+31)k+30$. This is the squared norm that becomes one trial's nonnegative estimator numerator.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/NormLoop.lean, line 21; source snapshot SHA-256 77b0cfcacb31de124df72256f83135e03208500fcb5037aea483ed0cbd93ec8e.

